## 24. EXPLICIT NON-GOALS

Do not:

- Treat subtitle generation as ASR.
- Treat text segmentation as forced alignment.
- Fabricate word timestamps.
- Invent speaker identities.
- Delete words to meet a line-length target without authorization.
- Change verbatim text silently.
- Treat a structurally valid subtitle file as proof of readability.
- Claim all players render Persian identically.
- Claim accessibility compliance without a defined evaluation.
- Claim native host subtitle integration without testing the actual host.
- Overwrite user-edited subtitle revisions.
- Hide information lost by export conversion.
- Upload transcripts or audio without authorization.

## 25. ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

Mark `VERIFIED` only when:

1. SHAHAB-025 timing capability is verified or limitations are explicitly respected.
2. SHAHAB-026 speaker capability is verified or speaker labels are disabled.
3. A canonical subtitle document schema exists.
4. Persian-aware segmentation is implemented.
5. Acoustic and display timing remain separate.
6. Reading-speed calculation is documented and tested.
7. RTL and mixed-script behavior is tested.
8. ZWNJ and Unicode integrity are preserved.
9. Speaker-aware captions work where supported.
10. Overlapping speech is represented honestly.
11. Export formats are validated.
12. Information loss is documented.
13. Manual editing is revisioned and reversible.
14. Stale transcript/alignment/diarization results are rejected.
15. Avapardaz integration works with the existing editor and persistence system.
16. Target-host compatibility is established by real tests or explicitly limited.
17. Automated QA is implemented.
18. Human evaluation is performed where required.
19. Performance is measured on large inputs.
20. Privacy and source identity remain intact.

A `VERIFIED` result may cover a restricted set of export formats or host applications, but the supported scope must be explicit.

